head
  title About
  meta(name="description" content="Kévyn, a full-stack developer from Bordeaux: how I got into coding, and what I care about in it.")
article.mx-auto.max-w-2xl
  h1.mb-10.text-3xl.font-semibold About
  .prose
    p I'm Kévyn, a full-stack developer from Bordeaux, France. I build web apps for a living, and Minecraft mods, tools and Godot projects for fun.
    h2 How I got here
    p It started with an Arduino, discovered at a family meal when I was twelve. I spent a year playing with it, then drifted to the screen: some very basic HTML, Discord bots hosted on Glitch, and a lot of Processing.
    p Processing came back in seconde, my first year of high school, when a class asked us to use it. I handed in a platform game, and the teacher had a hard time believing I had made it myself, though one look at the code would have settled it: it was a mess that would burn my eyes today. Around the same time, I wrote a Discord bot for a YouTuber, who paid for a VPS so I could run it there.
    p A friend had bought me a VPS of my own early on, and it helped a lot at my computer science IUT, where, I admit, I spent more classes than I should have playing Dofus. A one-year work-study web degree followed (licence pro en alternance), and right after it, the job I've now held for four years.
    h2 What I care about
    p Developer experience, performance and accessibility, and the footprint of what I build: the smaller it is, the less it costs, both to the people using it and to the planet.
    p I'm also picky about code itself, and about formatting most of all: code should breathe. I started #[a(href="https://github.com/Kayno0o/eslint") my own ESLint ruleset] as a layer over antfu's, and ended up rewriting it from scratch. At work, I set up a very strict PHP CS Fixer config, half to annoy my coworkers, half so I stop grumbling when I read their code.
